# git-credential-rhorizon, host → secret-name mapping
#
# Each line maps a Git server hostname to the rhorizon secret holding the
# matching credential (a Gitea / GitHub / GitLab API token, an HTTPS push
# password, etc.). The secret name is resolved against the namespaces the
# vault token is scoped to, there is no `namespace=` query parameter on
# the GET, so the token's `namespaces` claim is what makes the lookup
# unambiguous.
#
# Format
# ------
#   <git-host> = <secret-name>
#
# Lines starting with `#` and blank lines are ignored. Whitespace around
# `=` is stripped.
#
# Default
# -------
# If a host is not listed here, the helper looks up
#   git/<host-with-dots-as-dashes>-api-token
# So `gitea.example.com` resolves to `git/gitea-example-com-api-token`
# unless overridden below. Useful for fleets of repos sharing one
# convention; explicit overrides take priority.
#
# Examples
# --------
gitea.example.com   = gitea-api-token
github.com          = github-personal-access-token
gitlab.example.org  = gitlab-deploy-token
codeberg.org        = codeberg-token
